  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `set_part_axes` (`crates/app/src/mcp/align_tools.rs`) now builds `AlignPartToSetup::align_from_axes`, the same undoable command the Setups page's \"Part axes\" Apply queues (`CommandKind::AlignPartFromAxes`, #769 / PR #770). One undo step.\n  - One axis: the command falls back to the in-plane turn (#557); the reply is unchanged (`turn_deg`), plus `frame: \"in_plane\"`.\n  - Both +Y and +X: the picks' 3D directions define the full frame - primary lands exactly, the other is made square, +Z on the right-hand cross. Reply `frame: \"full_3d\"`, `turn_deg: null`. A left-handed pair is honoured literally (the part lands on its head), as the GUI does, instead of being refused.\n- Tool description and the camcraft-mcp skill row (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`) updated; `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 45 -> 46 (process file changed).\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/1329-mcp-align-from-axes.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New suite `crates/app/tests/mcp_align_axes.rs`: `set_part_axes_with_both_axes_aligns_the_full_3d_frame`. It pins a vertical edge as +Y with a top edge as +X: old +Z runs +Y, old +X stays +X, old -Y becomes the top. It also pins the left-handed pair: both picks land, and the old top faces -Z. It checks that undo restores the setup in one step, that one axis keeps `in_plane` with a 90-degree `turn_deg`, and that parallel picks are refused by name (\"along each other\").\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: ok (app lib, mcp_align_axes, mcp_setup), 16 s. `align_axes` (9/9) also passes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test mcp_align_axes --test mcp_setup --test align_axes -- -D warnings`: clean. A full `--all-targets` clippy run cannot build `crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs`, because upstream main's Tool literal there is missing the new `cutting` field. That is main's own build break, tracked as #1345 and fixed in a separate PR; this branch does not touch it.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- GUI hand check (no GUI code changed; the GUI already uses this command).\n- Seen while testing and not changed here: re-applying the same two-axis picks is not refused as \"already holds the part that way\". The composed alignment differs from the held one only by float noise, and `change_of` compares exactly. The GUI path behaves the same, so this is follow-up material rather than a regression.\n\nChangelog: MCP `set_part_axes` with both +Y and +X picked now aligns the part's full 3D frame as the Setups page does (a left-handed pair is honoured, not refused) (#1329)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; branch merges upstream/main.\n\nFixes #1329\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
